{
  "id": "Lyo.Google.Geolocation.Client",
  "name": "Lyo.Google.Geolocation.Client",
  "area": "Integration",
  "tagline": "Google Maps REST client and `IGeolocationService` implementation.",
  "description": "Google Maps REST client and `IGeolocationService` implementation.\n\n**Archetype C** — `Integration/Google/` (vendor folder). Geolocation is not Communication; this package mirrors `Lyo.Endato.Client` + Core store, not `Lyo.Translation.Google`. Path confirmed in [package layout](../../../docs/package-layout.md) (Phase 1).\n\nReferences [`Lyo.Geolocation`](../../../Core/Geolocation/Lyo.Geolocation/README.md) and [`Lyo.Geolocation.Models`](../../../Core/Geolocation/Lyo.Geolocation.Models/README.md) only — **not** `Lyo.Geolocation.Postgres`. The host wires this client together with the store.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Consumer composition",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPostgresGeolocationStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddGoogleMapsClientFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddGoogleMapsGeolocationService();\n\n// Worker/API: geocode, then persist\nvar result = await geolocationService.GeocodeAsync(query, ct);\nawait geolocationStore.SaveAddressAsync(result.Address, ct);"
    }
  ],
